Article 14
The obligations and responsibilities of the community as referred to in Article 12 letter b, shall be implemented in the form of community participation.
Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1), includes: the establishment of family partners at the kelurahan level;
the establishment of women's protection units within community organizations;
the implementation of independent socialization of women's rights;
the provision of first aid to victims; and reporting to the competent authorities if violence against victims occurs in their environment.
Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be carried out by individuals, social community institutions, non-governmental organizations, educational institutions, religious institutions, the private sector, and mass media.

Article 21
To prevent the occurrence of violence against women, the government carries out empowerment and awareness-raising for families, parents, and the community by providing information, guidance and/or outreach.
In addition to empowerment and awareness-raising as referred to in paragraph (1), the government undertakes efforts as follows:
a. increasing the quantity and quality of education, both formal and non-formal and informal;
b. opening accessibility to obtain education, training, funding, income enhancement, and social services;
c. opening employment opportunities for women;
d. building community participation and concern to implement prevention and protection of women from violence;
e. building and providing a complete and easily accessible information system;
f. building networks and cooperation with law enforcement apparatus, government apparatus, universities, and various non-governmental organizations that work and/or care about women; and
g. opening complaint posts for the protection of women from violence.

Article 13
The Regional Government implements efforts to protect women victims of violence through:
a. policies, programs, and activities for the protection of women victims of violence;
b. establishment of PPT;
c. ease of service to victims;
d. pursuing effectiveness and efficiency for the victim recovery process; and
e. cooperation and coordination in victim recovery efforts.
In order to carry out the obligations and responsibilities as referred to in paragraph (1) letter b, the regional government establishes programs and action activities for the protection of women in 1 (one) Regional Action Plan as a basis for regional apparatus in implementing protection for women victims of violence.
The Regional Action Plan as referred to in paragraph (2), constitutes part of the Regional Medium-Term Development Plan (RPJMD).
The Regional Action Plan as referred to in paragraph (2), is further regulated by Mayor Regulation.

Article 3
The objectives of implementing protection for women victims of violence are to:
1. prevent violence against women, including human trafficking;
2. eliminate all forms of violence and exploitation against women;
3. protect and provide a sense of security for women;
4. provide services to women victims of violence, reporters, and witnesses; and
5. facilitate and mediate household disputes to realize the integrity of a harmonious and prosperous household.
The objectives of implementing protection for women victims of violence as referred to in paragraph (1) include aspects of:
1. prevention;
2. services and assistance;
3. reunification; and
4. empowerment.

Article 22
Prevention of the occurrence of violence against women as referred to in Article 21, is implemented by regional apparatus whose duties and functions are in the fields of: social;
health;
education;
manpower;
women's empowerment and child protection;
mental and spiritual; and peace and order.
Prevention of violence by regional apparatus as referred to in paragraph (1), is implemented in an integrated and continuous manner based on the Regional Action Plan.

Article 2
The implementation of protection for women victims of violence, is carried out based on the principles of: justice;
gender equality; and non-discrimination.

REGIONAL REGULATION OF BIMA CITY
NUMBER 6 YEAR 2018
CONCERNING
PROTECTION OF WOMEN VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE
BY THE GRACE OF GOD ALMIGHTY
MAYOR OF BIMA,

Considering: a. that every citizen has the right to be free from torture or treatment that degrades human dignity and has the right to obtain security and freedom from all forms of violence;
b. that all forms of violence against women constitute violations of human rights so that their dignity and honor need to be protected and their right to life guaranteed in accordance with their nature and natural role without discrimination;
c. that based on the considerations as referred to in letters a and b, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning Protection of Women Victims of Violence;

In View of: 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
2. Law Number 69 Year 1958 concerning the Establishment of Level II Regions Within Level I Regions of Bali, West Nusa Tenggara and East Nusa Tenggara (State Gazette Year 1958 Number 122, Supplement to State Gazette Number 1655);
3. Law Number 7 Year 1984 concerning Ratification of the Convention on the Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination Against Women (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1984 Number 29, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3277);
4. Law Number 39 Year 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1999 Number 165, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia 3886);
5. Law Number 13 Year 2002 concerning the Establishment of Bima City in West Nusa Tenggara Province (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2002 Number 26, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4188);
6. Law Number 13 Year 2003 concerning Manpower (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2003 Number 39, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia 4279);
7. Law Number 23 Year 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2004 Number 95, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia 4419);
8. Law Number 39 Year 2004 concerning Placement and Protection of Indonesian Workers Abroad (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2004 Number 137, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4447);
9. Law Number 13 Year 2006 concerning Protection of Witnesses and Victims (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2006 Number 64, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4636);
10. Law Number 21 Year 2007 concerning Eradication of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2007 Number 58, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4720);
11. Law Number 11 Year 2009 concerning Social Welfare (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2009 Number 12, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4976);
12. Law Number 12 Year 2011 concerning Formation of Legislation (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2011 Number 82, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5234);
13. Law Number 23 Year 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2014 Number 244, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as has been amended several times most recently by Law Number 9 Year 2015 (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2015 Number 58, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5659);
14. Government Regulation Number 4 Year 2006 concerning Implementation and Cooperation for Recovery of Victims of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2006 Number 15, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia number 64);
15. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 2 Year 2008 concerning Implementation of Protection of Women;
16. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 01 Year 2010 concerning Minimum Service Standards (SPM) for Integrated Services for Women and Child Victims of Violence (State News of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2010 Number 56);
17. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 5 Year 2010 concerning Guidelines for Establishment and Development of Integrated Service Centers;
18. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 19 Year 2011 concerning Empowerment of Women Victims of Violence;

With Mutual Approval

Article 25
Forms of services provided to women victims of violence include: complaint services;
health services;
legal assistance;
repatriation;
rehabilitation, social reintegration, and medicolegal;
identification services; and psychological services.
Forms of services as referred to in paragraph (1) are implemented in accordance with minimum service standards established by the government and implemented by regional apparatus whose duties and functions are in the fields of: social;
health;
women's empowerment and protection; and mental and spiritual.
In carrying out duties and functions as referred to in paragraph (2), the Regional Government cooperates with government agencies, the provincial government, other district/city governments, and the community.
Further provisions regarding service procedures and the handling of women victims of violence as referred to in paragraph (1) are regulated by a Mayor's Regulation.

CHAPTER II
FORMS OF VIOLENCE
